package assets

/// The stored media reference (url + mime) — a contained value.
class MediaReference {
    String url
    String mimeType
}

/// A media-bearing record. `contains` alone makes MediaReference a value
/// object (its rows nest in `asset_photo`); Asset itself is the entity —
/// the object the media route family addresses.
class Asset {
    String name
    contains MediaReference[0..1] photo
}

/// A root record — the parent of `Contact` below. Media on a root entity is
/// the flat shape the Asset legs above already cover; Person exists to be the
/// NESTED anchor (issue #722).
class Person {
    String name
}

/// A CHILD record with its own media field: `router.tera` mounts its routes
/// under `/{person_id}/contacts`, so the media handler must extract the
/// ancestor tuple and prove the row belongs to the URL parent (issue #722).
class Contact {
    String name
    refers Person person
    contains MediaReference[0..1] avatar
}
